discussion about the differences between requests and orders,
which I don't think we need to have again. I had a similar discussion,
which I initiated, with the people who DO make policy here (who don't
read netnews, and whose attitude was that I shouldn't worry about the
net because it was, in their words, mostly noise. They also felt that
we should not *institute* any policy and they approved 100% of my
actions.) 

The upshot was, it wasn't a policy, it was a request, and one which
the student could have rejected. Had I realized that I was posting for
posterity, I would have said something like "our ad-hoc procedure has
been" instead of "our policy is"

There have been no complaints about censorship by any users, 
staff, or   administrators at my site, and this is a site
where users feel VERY free to complain and do so without
repercussions, judging from the volume of complaints we get about disk
space limitations, database performance, netnews expiration times,
