strictly 'gay or lesbian' and no other sexual practice. By implying other
sexual behaviors could be called a 'sexual preference', the HR person argued,
I was degrading this gay's lifestyle and harassing him in the workplace.

After asking how I could know the boundary line between legitimate comment
and discussion and harassment, the HR person told me that recent precedent
made any unwelcome comments harassing.  And that the protected minority
defines what is unwelcome.

And this Tartuffian drama was at Apple Computer -- one of the presumably
more enlightened hi-tech employers.
