In alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk there is an unfolding drama to do with 
harassment related to the existence of pornographic material in Usenet 
newsgroups, and also to its display.

The woman pushing for the ban on certain newsgroups is not part of the 
discussion (I think she is on holiday) and apparently is not familiar 
with Usenet.  At the other extreme, some defenders of freedom have 
derided her position in ways which made me chuckle for a moment but 
will certainly upset her, and which will detract (in some people's 
eyes) from the credibility of the arguments against censorship.  I 
would be really upset if I had been attacked in these unfair ways - 
especially if it was in my absence.

Arguments are being conducted about the morality, practicality and 
desirability of censorship of encoded data. People are aguing about 
what harassment is and whether a pin-up of a sexually alluring woman 
should be regarded any differently from such a woman in the flesh.  Is 
it the sexy pin-up, or the actions of the pinner-up that constitute 
harassment? People are deriding others for being radical feminists 
etc. etc. Some contributors are behaving like cowboys - as well they 
might in an academic -freedom.talk newsgroup. 

In the middle of this are people trying to understand the problem, and 
find solutions which provide privacy and freedom whilst trying to 
ensure freedom from harassment.

Feminist issues are being discussed in this thread, but apparently in 
the absence of feminists.  Perhaps alt.feminist veterans have seen it 
all before, but I am a newbie here, and I find it interesting. I am 
not suggesting that a pose of feminists ride over the hill to 
spiflicate the varmints, but I thought that some people in this 
newsgroup might be interested in this skirmish, in which some people 
and ideals will probably be hurt.

I think it is impossible to stop even the most horrible data being 
stored on computer carrying news, so there is no technological 
fix for the problem.  Solutions, if they are to be found, must be in 
the human domain.  That will not be easy - especially when the freedom 
of all (including cowboys) is being defended in the same forum in 
which cowboys publicly harass the woman who is complaining about 
harassment. 

