Of course the subject matter contributes, her just being alive
contributes, the internet contributes, but the blame lies wholly
with the harassers. 

The internet is a very large group of people.  With a corresponding huge
bell-shaped curve of opinion and education and manner. No matter
what idea you offer where someone will probably flame you for it.
At one time virtually 100% of my posts engendered at least one flame.
Sometimes more than a dozen. Sometimes obscene or threatening.

Writing on usenet takes some getting used to because of this. It
probably as close to 'public life' as many of us are likely to get.
But while trying it is also as close we are to get a full measure of
feedback on our contributions. For me, the breadth of comments makes up 
in full for the flamage.  The threatening or obscene mail I handle
immediately and separately.

