>I would try to phrase the last condition in terms of keeping
>postings in a forum relevant to the interests of that forum.  And
>there should be punishment for repeated violation of this.

No!  Off-topic posting alone should not be actionable, no matter how often
one does it.  It should be subject to sanctions only if it both violates any
reasonable expectation of encountering it in the place where it's posted,
_and_ is offensive at face value to those likely to encounter it there (the
conditions which the proposed policy seems to actually be alluding to) or
else causes either some other type of substantive nuisance, or interference
with the technical functioning of the news system (as some observers asserted
that Robert McElwaine's posts did).

